# "For each Faerie you control" is a word of Spell Stutter's text (CR 612.2): Bot1 casts Artificial Evolution on its own Stutter
# in response to nothing but its own cast, replacing Faerie with Human, so the Stutter now charges {1} for each Human Bot1
# controls - the Dragon Sniper (a Human Archer) - and the price is {3}. Bot2 has only Mox Pearl and Mox Emerald left after
# paying for the Bolt, which would pay the unchanged {2} (see the sibling scenarios), but cannot pay {3}: the Bolt is
# countered and Bot1 stays at 20.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Emerald
Dragon Sniper
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Spell Stutter
Artificial Evolution
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Lightning Bolt
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dragon Sniper.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spell Stutter.Cast(Stack.Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Artificial Evolution.Cast(Stack.Spell Stutter)
Bot1.Modes(Faerie)
Bot1.Modes(Human)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Dragon Sniper.Subtypes = Archer; Human
! Bot2.PayCost
Bot2.Decline
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Graveyard = Spell Stutter; Artificial Evolution
